    "title": "Did 'Marty Supreme' or Timothée Chalamet win any Oscars in 2026?",
    "text": "March 15, 2026Updated March 16, 2026, 12:56 a.m. ET\"Marty Supreme\" may have started the award season on a high, with star Timothée Chalamet scoring two back-to-back wins, but it evidently lost steam by the time the Oscars rolled around.Director Josh Safdie’s adventurous historical comedy, which had earned nine nods and was in running for the night's biggest prize – best picture – alongside \"Sinners,\" \"The Secret Agent\", and \"Blue Moon, “Bugonia,” \"F1: The Movie,\" “Frankenstein,” “Hamnet,” “One Battle After Another,\" “Sentimental Value” and “Train Dreams\" failed to score at the 98th Academy Awards in Los Angeles.The film's star, however, got plenty of attention during the ceremony, and was mocked multiple times for his controversial comments about ballet and opera.\"Security is extremely tight tonight,\" host Conan O'Brien said in his monologue. \"I'm told there's concerns about attacks from both the opera and ballet communities.\"Chalamet had drawn criticism from the arts community in recent weeks for saying \"no one cares\" about ballet and opera during a sit-down with Matthew McConaughey.USA TODAY's Movie Meter 2026: Vote for the best film of the yearHow many Academy Awards did 'Marty Supreme' win?\"Marty Supreme\" won none of the nine awards it was nominated for during Sunday's ceremony. The film was nominated in following categories, but did not take home any trophies:Best pictureBest original screenplayBest cinematographyBest editingBest actor (Timothée Chalamet)Best director (Josh Safdie)Best casting (Jennifer Venditti)Best costume design (Miyako Bellizzi)Best production designWhat is 'Marty Supreme'?Set in 1950s Manhattan, \"Marty Supreme\" follows a fast-talking ping-pong hotshot named Marty Mauser (Chalamet), who is dead set on jetting to Tokyo to compete in the global championships. But first, he needs to scrounge up money and get sponsors, which lands him in a series of violent, get-rich-quick schemes. According to the film's synopsis, Marty is \"a young man with a dream no one respects,\" who \"goes to hell and back in pursuit of greatness.\"The cast of \"Marty Supreme\" includes:Timothée Chalamet as Marty MauserGwyneth Paltrow as Kay StoneKoto Kawaguchi as Koto EndoOdessa A’zion as RachelTyler Okonma (Tyler, The Creator) as WallyKevin O’Leary as Milton RockwellUSA TODAY movie critic Brian Truitt gave the film ★★★½ out of four, writing \"director Josh Safdie’s globetrotting, genre-busting comedy thriller is a proudly oddball period movie that boasts throwback elements but leans timeless in its unlikely hero’s journey.\"Contributing: Patrick Ryan, Brian Truitt, Brendan Morrow / USA TODAYSaman Shafiq is a trending news reporter for USA TODAY. Reach her at sshafiq@usatodayco.com and follow her on X and Instagram @saman_shafiq7.",
